{
  "title": "iOS: restore shopping list scroll position after termination",
  "description": "Follow-up to restoring recipe scroll position after background termination (RecipePlace.scrollAnchor and RecipeScrollRestorationModifier in ramekin-ios/Ramekin/RecipeDetailView.swift). \
The shopping list still reopens at the top when iOS kills the app in the background. \
It's a List (ShoppingListView.itemsList) grouped by category with a checked section, so the recipe detail's preference-key tracker doesn't carry over directly: List rows are lazy, so only rendered rows report positions, and an item id can move between groups when checked. \
Likely approach: track the topmost visible item id via row onAppear/onDisappear or the same preference key inside the List, keep it in a ContentView @SceneStorage key (scene storage keys must be unique per scene), and ScrollViewReader.scrollTo it once ShoppingListStore has loaded items; drop it if the item is gone. \
Shopping lists are usually short, so this is low value; extend RecipeFlowTests.testRelaunchAfterTerminationRestoresPlace if it lands.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
